{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he shall bear his iniquity.</b> The Sages of blessed memory already stated (Yoma, chapter Yom HaKippurim) that this speaks of the suspended guilt-offering (אָשָׁם תָּלוּי) — one who does not know whether he sinned or not. Concerning this it says <b>and he shall bear his iniquity</b> according to what is fitting for him: whether he sinned inadvertently, or no sin occurred but his iniquity was that he did not guard himself so that he fell into doubt — according to his iniquity he shall bear the punishment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The citation 'יומא פרק יום הכפורים' refers to the chapter in tractate Yoma titled Yom HaKippurim; resolved per standard Talmudic citation convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:49.498726897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}